#3220
On the River.~
The river has slowed to a quiet crawl.  The green moss covers
the entire surface of the river.  The gray moss hangs from the
limbs of the dying trees, stretching to the ground and touching
the water's surface around the edges of the river.  You realize
you are traveling through a swamp of some sort.  The banks are 
layered with a small pathe of fog.  The river continues to the
east and west.
~
